      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\(G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1|\\) by first determining where the absolute value expressions change their behavior, which are at \\(x = -1\\) and \\(x = 1\\). We can break the problem into three intervals: \\(x < -1\\), \\(-1 \\leq x < 1\\), and \\(x \\geq 1\\).\n\n**Step 1: Define the function in each interval.**\n\n1. **For \\(x < -1\\):**\n   \\[\n   G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| = -(x+1) - (-(x-1)) = -x-1 + x-1 = -2\n   \\]\n   So, for \\(x < -1\\), \\(G(x) = -2\\).\n\n2. **For \\(-1 \\leq x < 1\\):**\n   \\[\n   G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| = (x+1) - (-(x-1)) = x+1 + x-1 = 2x\n   \\]\n   So, for \\(-1 \\leq x < 1\\), \\(G(x) = 2x\\).\n\n3. **For \\(x \\geq 1\\):**\n   \\[\n   G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| = (x+1) - (x-1) = x+1 - x + 1 = 2\n   \\]\n   So, for \\(x \\geq 1\\), \\(G(x) = 2\\).\n\n**Step 2: Determine the range of the function.**\n\nFrom the expressions derived in the intervals, we can see that:\n- For \\(x < -1\\), \\(G(x) = -2\\).\n- For \\(-1 \\leq x < 1\\), \\(G(x) = 2x\\) ranges from \\(-2\\) to \\(2\\).\n- For \\(x \\geq 1\\), \\(G(x) = 2\\).\n\nCombining these results, the minimum value of \\(G(x)\\) is \\(-2\\) and the maximum value is \\(2\\). Therefore, the range of the function \\(G(x)\\) is \\([-2, 2]\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{[-2, 2]}\n\\]",
